SickOS 1.2 — Penetration Testing Report

Target: SickOS 1.2 — VulnHub Lab
Assessment Type: Internal Network Penetration Test
Attacker Machine: Kali Linux
Target IP: 192.168.1.100
Attacker IP: 192.168.1.50
Objective: Obtain initial access to the target, escalate privileges, and retrieve the root-level challenge flag.

1. Executive Summary

This assessment was conducted against the intentionally vulnerable SickOS 1.2 virtual machine in an isolated lab environment.

The assessment demonstrated a complete attack chain beginning with network reconnaissance and service enumeration and ending with root-level access.

The primary attack path was:

Network Discovery → Port Scanning → HTTP/WebDAV Enumeration → Unauthenticated File Upload → Remote Shell → Local Enumeration → chkrootkit Privilege Escalation → Root Access

The most significant finding was an improperly configured HTTP service that permitted unauthenticated PUT requests to the /test/ directory. This allowed an attacker to upload a server-side script and obtain command execution on the target.

After obtaining access as the low-privileged www-data account, further local enumeration identified an outdated chkrootkit installation vulnerable to a known local privilege-escalation condition. Exploiting this allowed escalation from www-data to root.

